{
  "description": "Language-agnostic laws of the analysis.measure geometry widgets. Shapes are recipes (box, sphere, cylinder, translate, rotate, cut, compound, vertex, face and edge picked by outward normal or end points, curvedFace, curvedEdge, rectangleWire) that Rust builds with the kernel and TypeScript rebuilds with manifold-3d and three. A box has one corner at the origin and spans its size along x, y and z; a sphere is centered at the origin; a cylinder stands on the XY plane along +Z. Selections name faces by outward normal. Outputs match to `tolerance` (absolute, relative above magnitude one) against the analytic values of the kernel; the oracle recomputes them from triangle meshes to `oracleTolerance` (default 1e-6 for flat shapes). `unchecked` lists output ports that must be present but have no unique value.",
